## Authentication

The scaffold ships Django REST Framework's default authenticators — **session
cookie** and **HTTP Basic**. Every endpoint requires an authenticated user unless
its view opts out with an explicit `permission_classes` declaration.

Session (browser, same-origin — what the frontend uses):

```
Cookie: sessionid=<session-id>
X-CSRFToken: <csrf-token>
```

HTTP Basic (scripts and `curl`):

```
Authorization: Basic <base64(username:password)>
```

Create a user with `dude db superuser`, then log in at `/admin/` to get a session.

